Second Order Derivatives","answers":[{"id":62304419,"created":"2026-10-15T21:21:27.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"-3\"]","timeElapsed":21225,"number":1,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 9:21 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:21","question":{"id":342851,"format":"FR","difficulty":3,"exampleId":3653,"text":"Find $g''(1)$ if $g(x) =  -x^3  + 4x\\sqrt{x}.$","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" ","choice4":" ","choice5":" ","freeAnswerChoice":" \\newline\n$g''(1)=$ \n[\n    answer: -3;\n    type: number;\n    width: 40;\n    margin-left: 2;\n    margin-right: 1;\n    buttons: frac, sqrt, nrt;\n]","explanation":"<p>Computing the first derivative, we have\n\\[\n\\begin{align}\ng'(x) &= \\left(-x^3  + 4x\\sqrt{x} \\right)' \\\\[5pt]\n&=   \\left(-x^3+4x^{3/2} \\right)' \\\\[5pt]\n&=  3(-x^2) +\\dfrac 32 \\left(4x^{1/2}\\right)\\\\[3pt]\n&= -3x^2+ 6x^{1/2}.\n\\end{align}\n\\]\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\\[\n\\begin{align}\ng''(x) &=   \\left(-3x^2+ 6x^{1/2} \\right)' \\\\[5pt]\n&= 2(-3x) +  \\dfrac 12 \\left(6x^{-1/2}\\right)\\\\[5pt]\n&=  -6x + 3x^{-1/2}\\\\[5pt]\n&= -6x+\\dfrac3{{\\sqrt{x}}} .\n\\end{align}\n\\]</p>\n<p>Finally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=1$, we obtain\n\\[\n\\begin{align}\ng''(1) &= - 6(1)+\\dfrac3{{\\sqrt{1}}}\\\\[5pt]\n&=  -6+ 3\\\\[5pt]\n&= \\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{-3}. \n\\end{align}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":281,"name":"Second and Higher-Order Derivatives"},"example":{"id":3653,"title":"Computing Second Order Derivatives"},"group":{"id":95369,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14250685,"answer":{"id":62304419,"cread":"2026-10-15T21:21:27.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["-3"],"timeElapsed":21225},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"newline":true},{"text":"$g''(1)=$ \n"},{"textbox":{"answer":"-3","type":"number","width":40,"margin":{"left":2,"right":1},"buttons":["frac","sqrt","nrt"]}}]},"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62304443,"created":"2026-10-15T21:22:03.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":26587,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 9:22 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:27","question":{"id":10892,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":3653,"text":"<p>Find $f''(-2)$ if $f(x) = 2x^3 + 4x^2 - 7.$</p>\n","choice1":"$-16$","choice2":"$16$","choice3":"$21$","choice4":"$-21$","choice5":"$18$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Computing the first derivative, we have\n\\[\n\\begin{align}\n \tf'(x)\t  &= \\left(2x^3 + 4x^2 - 7\\right)' & \\\\\n \t\t  &=  3\\cdot 2x^2 +2\\cdot 4x-0  \\\\\n \t          & = 6x^2 + 8x \\,.\\\\\n\\end{align}\n\\]</p>\n<p>Computing the second derivative, we have\n\\[\n\\begin{align}\n  \tf''(x)   & = \\left(6x^2+8x\\right)' \\\\\n \t\t   &= 2\\cdot 6x + 8  \\\\\n \t\t   & =12x + 8  \\,.  \\\\\n\\end{align}\n\\]</p>\n<p>Finally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=-2$, we obtain\n\\[\n\\begin{align}\n   \tf''(-2)    & = 12(-2) + 8 \\\\\n \t \t   & =-24 + 8 \\\\\n \t\t   & = -16. \\\\\n \t\n\\end{align}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":281,"name":"Second and Higher-Order Derivatives"},"example":{"id":3653,"title":"Computing Second Order Derivatives"},"group":{"id":95365,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14250685,"answer":{"id":62304443,"cread":"2026-10-15T21:22:03.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":26587},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":3654,"number":2,"title":"Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibniz Notation","answers":[{"id":62304467,"created":"2026-10-15T21:22:34.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12558,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 9:22 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":105266,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":3654,"text":"<p>Calculate $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}^2y}{\\textrm{d}x^2}$ for $y = 7x - 4x^2.$</p>\n","choice1":"$- 8$","choice2":"$1- 8x$","choice3":"$7- 8x$","choice4":"$- 9$","choice5":"$- 7$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Computing the first derivative, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n \t\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}  \n\t\t &=  \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left(7x - 4x^2\\right) \\\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 7 - 2\\cdot 4x  \\\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 7- 8x  .  \n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Computing the second derivative, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n \t\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}^2y}{\\textrm{d}x^2}  \n\t\t &= \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left (7- 8x\\right ) \\\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 0 - 8\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= - 8.  \n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":281,"name":"Second and Higher-Order Derivatives"},"example":{"id":3654,"title":"Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibniz Notation"},"group":{"id":95384,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14250685,"answer":{"id":62304467,"cread":"2026-10-15T21:22:34.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12558},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62304481,"created":"2026-10-15T21:22:51.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"6-\\\\frac{8}{x^3}\"]","timeElapsed":12773,"number":4,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 9:22 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":342877,"format":"FR","difficulty":1,"exampleId":3654,"text":"Calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}^2y}{\\textrm{d}x^2}$ for $\ny = \\dfrac{6x^3 + 2x^2 - 8}{2x}.$","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" ","choice4":" ","choice5":" ","freeAnswerChoice":"\\newline\n$\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}^2y}{\\textrm{d}x^2}=$ \n[\n    answer:6 -\\dfrac{8}{x^{3}};\n    type: expression;\n    width: 80;\n    margin-left: 2;\n    margin-right: 1;\n    buttons: frac, exp;\n]\n\n","explanation":"<p>Computing the first derivative, we get\n\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left(\\dfrac{6x^3 + 2x^2 - 8}{2x} \\right)\\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left( 3x^2 + x -4x^{-1} \\right)\\\\[5pt]\n&= 6x +1 +(-1)(-4x^{-2})\\\\[5pt]\n&= 6x +1 +4x^{-2}.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Computing the second derivative, we get\n\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}^2y}{\\textrm{d}x^2} \n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left( 6x +1 +4x^{-2}\\right)\\\\[5pt]\n&= 6 +0 +(-2)(4x^{-3})\\\\[5pt]\n&= \\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{6 -\\dfrac{8}{x^{3}}}.\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":281,"name":"Second and Higher-Order Derivatives"},"example":{"id":3654,"title":"Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibniz Notation"},"group":{"id":95396,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14250685,"answer":{"id":62304481,"cread":"2026-10-15T21:22:51.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["6-\\frac{8}{x^3}"],"timeElapsed":12773},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"newline":true},{"text":"$\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}^2y}{\\textrm{d}x^2}=$ \n"},{"textbox":{"answer":"6 -\\dfrac{8}{x^{3}}","type":"expression","width":80,"margin":{"left":2,"right":1},"buttons":["frac","exp"]}}]},"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":3655,"number":3,"title":"Computing Higher Order Derivatives","answers":[{"id":62304505,"created":"2026-10-15T21:23:18.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14580,"number":5,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 9:23 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":104295,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":3655,"text":"<p>Given $f(x) = \\dfrac{5-x^4}{6x^2},$ find $f'''(x).$</p>\n","choice1":"$ -\\dfrac{20}{x^5} $","choice2":"$ \\dfrac{5}{x^4}  - \\dfrac{1}{3}$ ","choice3":"$- \\dfrac{5}{3x^3}  - \\dfrac{1}{3}$ ","choice4":"$- \\dfrac{10}{x^4}  - \\dfrac{x}{3}$ ","choice5":"$ 1-\\dfrac{20}{3x^5} $","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>First, notice that we can rewrite the function as follows:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\tf(x)\t&= \\dfrac{5-x^4}{6x^2}\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{5}{6x^2} - \\dfrac{x^2}{6}\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Now, computing the first derivative, we get\n\\begin{align}\n \t f'(x)\t&= \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left( \\dfrac{5}{6x^2} - \\dfrac{x^2}{6} \\right) \\\\[5pt]\n \t\t&= \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left( \\dfrac{5}{6}x^{-2} - \\dfrac{x^2}{6} \\right) \\\\[5pt]\n \t\t&= -\\dfrac{5}{3}x^{-3} -  \\dfrac{x }{3} . \n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Computing the second derivative, we get\n\\begin{align}\n \tf''(x)\t&= \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left( -\\dfrac{5}{3}x^{-3} -  \\dfrac{x }{3}\\right) \\\\[5pt]\n \t\t&= 5x^{-4} - \\dfrac{1}{3}.  \n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Finally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\\begin{align}\n \tf'''(x) &= \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left(   5x^{-4} - \\dfrac{1}{3}      \\right) \\\\[5pt]\t\n \t\t&= -20x^{-5}\\\\[5pt]\t\n \t\t&= -\\dfrac{20}{x^5}  . \t\t\t\t\t\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":281,"name":"Second and Higher-Order Derivatives"},"example":{"id":3655,"title":"Computing Higher Order Derivatives"},"group":{"id":95445,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14250685,"answer":{"id":62304505,"cread":"2026-10-15T21:23:18.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14580},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62304517,"created":"2026-10-15T21:23:34.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"-\\\\cos x\"]","timeElapsed":11246,"number":6,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 9:23 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:11","question":{"id":343087,"format":"FR","difficulty":1,"exampleId":3655,"text":"Given $f(x) = \\dfrac12 x^2 + \\sin x +3x,$ we have","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" ","choice4":" ","choice5":" ","freeAnswerChoice":"\\newline\n$f'''(x)=$ \n[\n    answer: -\\cos{x};\n    type: expression;\n    width: 60;\n    margin-left: 2;\n    margin-right: 1;\n    buttons: frac, exp, cos, sin;\n].\n","explanation":"<p>Computing the first derivative, we get\n\\begin{align}\n\tf'(x)\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left(  \\dfrac12 x^2 + \\sin x +3x\\right)\\\\[5pt]\n\t\n                &= x  + \\cos x +3. \n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Computing the second derivative, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\tf''(x)\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left( x  + \\cos x +3\\right)\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 1-\\sin x. \\\\[5pt]\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Finally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\\begin{align}\n \tf'''(x) &= \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left(  1-\\sin x  \\right) \\\\[5pt]\t\n&= \\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{-\\cos x}. \\\\[5pt]\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":281,"name":"Second and Higher-Order Derivatives"},"example":{"id":3655,"title":"Computing Higher Order Derivatives"},"group":{"id":95448,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14250685,"answer":{"id":62304517,"cread":"2026-10-15T21:23:34.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["-\\cos x"],"timeElapsed":11246},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"newline":true},{"text":"$f'''(x)=$ \n"},{"textbox":{"answer":"-\\cos{x}","type":"expression","width":60,"margin":{"left":2,"right":1},"buttons":["frac","exp","sin","cos"]}},{"text":"."}]},"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]}],"localGraph":{"topicId":281,"topics":[{"id":280,"name":"Differentiating Trigonometric Functions","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"h